\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {B.2}{\ignorespaces Halo-exchange latency from the participant calibration, on idle V100s across two nodes. Seven-repeat medians; payloads are the exchanges the solver performs at each grid and block width. Adding participants taxes the all-reduce (\Cref  {tab:ca-participants}) far more than it taxes the halo, which is a point-to-point exchange with a fixed neighbor.}}{52}{table.caption.82}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:app-halo}{{B.2}{52}{Halo-exchange latency from the participant calibration, on idle V100s across two nodes. Seven-repeat medians; payloads are the exchanges the solver performs at each grid and block width. Adding participants taxes the all-reduce (\Cref {tab:ca-participants}) far more than it taxes the halo, which is a point-to-point exchange with a fixed neighbor}{table.caption.82}{}}
