\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {B.3}{\ignorespaces The allocation model: largest odd grid admitted per topology and block width, from the device's reported free memory with a 10\% reserve, evaluated before any allocation was made. The selected common grid is the minimum over all sixteen arms, $n = 381$ (55{,}306{,}341 rows), whose one-V100 $s{=}4$ allocation was predicted to sit 173\,MiB below the reserve-limited capacity---and did allocate.}}{52}{table.caption.83}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:app-memory}{{B.3}{52}{The allocation model: largest odd grid admitted per topology and block width, from the device's reported free memory with a 10\% reserve, evaluated before any allocation was made. The selected common grid is the minimum over all sixteen arms, $n = 381$ (55{,}306{,}341 rows), whose one-V100 $s{=}4$ allocation was predicted to sit 173\,MiB below the reserve-limited capacity---and did allocate}{table.caption.83}{}}
