\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {B.4}{\ignorespaces The independent referee's canonical reference set, generated on an idle V100 with the fixed Al-Mohy--Higham Taylor action \cite  {almohy-higham-2011}. The Basket payoff's boundary forcing inflates the augmented one-norm, so the fixed contract selects an impractical substep count and a scaled variant is used instead; Rainbow has no forcing tail and keeps the fixed contract.}}{52}{table.caption.84}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:app-referee}{{B.4}{52}{The independent referee's canonical reference set, generated on an idle V100 with the fixed Al-Mohy--Higham Taylor action \cite {almohy-higham-2011}. The Basket payoff's boundary forcing inflates the augmented one-norm, so the fixed contract selects an impractical substep count and a scaled variant is used instead; Rainbow has no forcing tail and keeps the fixed contract}{table.caption.84}{}}
